---
import JoinForm from './JoinForm.astro';
---
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="nav" aria-label="Site">
  <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Tracend, back to top"><span data-mark></span><span translate="no">Tracend</span></a>
  <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Sections"><a href="#day" data-day-link>How it works</a><a href="#progress">Progress</a><a href="#complete">The app</a><a href="#demo">Try it</a></nav>
  <a class="nav-cta" href="#join" data-focus>Join the beta</a>
</header>

<div id="smooth-wrapper"><div id="smooth-content">
<main id="main">

  <section class="film" id="top" data-mode="flow" aria-labelledby="hero-h">
    <div class="f-stage">
      <div class="f-amb" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="f-copy">
        <p class="kicker"><i></i>Private beta. For iPhone, best with Apple Watch. Android in testing.</p>
        <h1 id="hero-h" class="disp">
          <span class="hl" data-hl="a"><span class="line">Set a goal.</span><span class="line">Tracend plans</span><span class="line">the rest.</span></span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lede">What pros get from a trainer and a nutritionist: a plan made for you, never a template. Training and food set from your goal, your body and your own data, read against your recovery every morning and adjusted so you <strong>stay on course</strong>. From the iPhone and Apple Watch you own.</p>
        <JoinForm id="e1" />
      </div>

      <div class="bridge" aria-hidden="true"><p>Week 12, Tuesday 07:02. Rewinding</p><h2 class="disp">How did it know? It started with a goal.</h2></div>

      <div class="f-dev" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="f-giant"><span class="f-gday mono" data-hday></span><span class="f-gclock" data-hclock></span></div>
        <div class="f-glow"></div>
        <div class="f-floor"></div>
        <div class="dev-rise"><div class="dev"><div class="dev-tilt"><div data-phone-slot></div></div></div></div>
        <div class="fc fc-train" data-fc="-1"><div class="fc-in"><div class="fc-core"><span class="k mono">Mon 18:40 &middot; Train</span><span class="v">120<small>kg</small> &times; 5<span class="pill">New best</span></span><span class="s">Back squat, set 5 of 5</span></div></div></div>
        <div class="fc fc-food" data-fc="-1"><div class="fc-in"><div class="fc-core"><span class="k mono">Mon 20:30 &middot; Dinner</span><span class="v">760<small>kcal</small></span><span class="s">52 g protein, from one photo</span></div></div></div>
        <div class="fc fc-sleep" data-fc="-1"><div class="fc-in"><div class="fc-core"><span class="k mono">Mon 23:10 &middot; Sleep</span><span class="v">6 h 12 m</span><span class="s">About an hour short</span></div></div></div>
        <div class="fc fc-coach" data-fc="1"><div class="fc-in"><div class="fc-core"><span class="k mono"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12"><path fill="#C8F05A" d="M6 .8l1.3 3.4 3.5.4-2.7 2.3.9 3.5L6 8.5 3 10.4l.9-3.5L1.2 4.6l3.5-.4z"/></svg>Tue 07:02 &middot; Coach</span><span class="v">Go lighter today.</span><span class="s">Deadlift 3 &times; 3 at 140 kg, effort 7 at most. You slept short after heavy legs.</span></div></div></div>
        <div class="callouts">
          <p class="co" data-co="g0" style="top:46%"><i></i><span><b>Your goal</b>Every answer shapes the plan.</span></p>
          <p class="co" data-co="g1" style="top:30%"><i></i><span><b>Your usual months</b>Not just last week.</span></p>
          <p class="co" data-co="g2" style="top:62%"><i></i><span><b>You approve it</b>Nothing starts until you do.</span></p>
          <p class="co" data-co="0" style="top:52%"><i></i><span><b>Set 5 of 5</b>New best, logged with its effort.</span></p>
          <p class="co" data-co="1" style="top:72%"><i></i><span><b>From one photo</b>An estimate. You check it, then confirm.</span></p>
          <p class="co" data-co="2" style="top:40%"><i></i><span><b>While you sleep</b>Your watch reads every stage.</span></p>
          <p class="co" data-co="3" style="top:42%"><i></i><span><b>Recovery 36</b>Each reading against your own normal.</span></p>
          <p class="co" data-co="4" style="top:56%"><i></i><span><b>Coach</b>Today&rsquo;s session, adjusted, with the reason.</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="f-story" id="day">
        <div class="day-head"><h2 class="sec-h disp" id="day-h"><span class="act-a">Week 1. Sam sets a goal.</span><span class="act-b">Week 12. The plan at work.</span></h2><p class="sec-sub">Follow an example athlete, Sam: the evening the plan was made, then one day twelve weeks in. These are the app&rsquo;s own screens, with example numbers.</p></div>
        <div class="clockbar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dc-day" data-dday></span><span class="dc-time" data-dclock></span></div>
        <ol class="beats">
          <li class="act-break" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mono">Week 1</span></li>
          <li class="beat" data-i="0"><p class="b-when sr-only">Week 1 &middot; Sun 21:14</p><h3>You set the goal.</h3><p class="l">Lose fat, keep strength: from 80.6 kg to 75. Then the days you can train, your equipment and anything to avoid.</p><p class="pf"><span class="pf-was"><em>Usually</em><s><span class="st">A template plan, the same for everyone.</span></s></span><span class="pf-now"><em>Tracend</em>A plan built for your goal and your week.</span></p><div class="b-phone"></div></li>
          <li class="beat" data-i="1"><p class="b-when sr-only">Week 1 &middot; Sun 21:19</p><h3>It gets to know you.</h3><p class="l">Your usual months from Apple Health, your current lifts, and up to three questions from the coach.</p><p class="pf"><span class="pf-was"><em>Usually</em><s><span class="st">A long form, then guesswork.</span></s></span><span class="pf-now"><em>Tracend</em>Your own data, and a coach&rsquo;s questions.</span></p><div class="b-phone"></div></li>
          <li class="beat" data-i="2"><p class="b-when sr-only">Week 1 &middot; Sun 21:23</p><h3>You approve the plan.</h3><p class="l">Twenty weeks, four days a week, starting loads, 2,600 kcal and 160 g protein a day, with the reasons. Nothing starts until you approve it.</p><p class="pf"><span class="pf-was"><em>Usually</em><s><span class="st">A plan you can&rsquo;t question.</span></s></span><span class="pf-now"><em>Tracend</em>Every number with its reason. Your call.</span></p><div class="b-phone"></div></li>
          <li class="act-break" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mono">12 weeks later</span></li>
          <li class="beat" data-i="3"><p class="b-when sr-only">Week 12 &middot; Mon 18:40</p><h3>You train.</h3><p class="l">Back squat, 5 sets of 5 at 120 kg. Every set logged with its effort. The last one is a new best.</p><p class="pf"><span class="pf-was"><em>Usually</em><s><span class="st">Sets scribbled in a notes app.</span></s></span><span class="pf-now"><em>Tracend</em>Every set logged, with its effort.</span></p><div class="b-phone"></div></li>
          <li class="beat" data-i="4"><p class="b-when sr-only">Week 12 &middot; Mon 20:30</p><h3>You eat.</h3><p class="l">One photo of dinner. Protein and calories land on your day, once you confirm them.</p><p class="pf"><span class="pf-was"><em>Usually</em><s><span class="st">Guessing macros in a food diary.</span></s></span><span class="pf-now"><em>Tracend</em>One photo. You confirm the numbers.</span></p><div class="b-phone"></div></li>
          <li class="beat" data-i="5"><p class="b-when sr-only">Week 12 &middot; Mon 23:10</p><h3>You sleep.</h3><p class="l">Your watch keeps reading. 6 h 12 m, about an hour less than you need.</p><p class="pf"><span class="pf-was"><em>Usually</em><s><span class="st">A sleep score, alone in another app.</span></s></span><span class="pf-now"><em>Tracend</em>Read right next to your training.</span></p><div class="b-phone"></div></li>
          <li class="beat" data-i="6"><p class="b-when sr-only">Week 12 &middot; Tue 06:45</p><h3>Your body answers.</h3><p class="l">Short sleep after a heavy day. Recovery 36, under-recovered, with the reasons spelled out.</p><p class="pf"><span class="pf-was"><em>Usually</em><s><span class="st">A recovery number, and no next step.</span></s></span><span class="pf-now"><em>Tracend</em>The reasons, spelled out.</span></p><div class="b-phone"></div></li>
          <li class="beat" data-i="7"><p class="b-when sr-only">Week 12 &middot; Tue 07:02</p><h3>Today, adjusted.</h3><p class="l">Lighter pulls today, so the week still moves Sam toward 75 kg without losing strength. The plan itself only changes when you approve it.</p><p class="pf"><span class="pf-was"><em>Usually</em><s><span class="st">The same plan, however you slept.</span></s></span><span class="pf-now"><em>Tracend</em>Today&rsquo;s session, adjusted, with why. Your plan waits for your OK.</span></p><div class="b-phone"></div>
            <div class="mini-cta"><a class="btn-ghost" href="#join" data-focus>Join the beta</a><p>Free. For iPhone, best with Apple Watch. Android in testing.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="rail" role="group" aria-label="Jump to a moment">
          <button type="button" data-go="0"><em class="rail-act">Week 1</em>21:14<span>Goal</span></button><button type="button" data-go="1">21:19<span>Learn</span></button><button type="button" data-go="2">21:23<span>Plan</span></button><button type="button" data-go="3" class="rail-gap"><em class="rail-act">Week 12</em>18:40<span>Train</span></button><button type="button" data-go="4">20:30<span>Eat</span></button><button type="button" data-go="5">23:10<span>Sleep</span></button><button type="button" data-go="6">06:45<span>Read</span></button><button type="button" data-go="7">07:02<span>Adjust</span></button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="sr-only">Illustration: the Tracend Today screen on a phone. Example athlete Sam, week 12 of a 20-week plan to lean down to 75 kilograms and keep strength. Tuesday morning: recovery 36, under-recovered. Around it, Monday's squat session, dinner and sleep, and the Coach's call: go lighter today, deadlift 3 by 3 at 140 kilograms.</p>
    <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-day-live></p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="progress" aria-labelledby="progress-h">
    <div class="pg">
      <div class="pg-copy">
        <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="progress-h">It checks your progress, like a coach would.</h2>
        <p class="sec-sub">Every week Tracend looks at the whole picture: your weight and measurements against the goal, your strength, how you trained and recovered. Then it shows where the plan should focus next.</p>
        <div class="nx-steps pg-steps" role="tablist" aria-label="Progress">
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-s="0"><b>01</b><span>Weight and measurements</span><em>Weigh in, and add your waist, chest, hips, arms and thighs if you like. A trend toward your goal, not daily noise.</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="1"><b>02</b><span>Strength, kept</span><em>Workouts done against planned, and your best lifts. On a cut, the proof you are keeping muscle.</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="2"><b>03</b><span>A weekly review</span><em>What you did, how you recovered, what stays the same and next week&rsquo;s focus. Calculated from your logs, no AI.</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="3"><b>04</b><span>Physique check</span><em>Private photos, front, side and back. An AI visual estimate of which muscles to bring up, which you can make your focus.</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
        </div>
        <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-pg-live></p>
      </div>
      <div class="pg-dev" aria-hidden="true" data-pg></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="you" aria-labelledby="you-h">
    <div class="ys">
      <div class="ys-copy">
        <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="you-h">Made for you. Never a template.</h2>
        <p class="sec-sub">Like a coach who has met you: your goal, age, body, training history, limits and your own Apple Health data set every number in the plan. A 22-year-old chasing size and a 45-year-old protecting a knee should never get the same week.</p>
        <div class="ys-mem">
          <p class="ys-mem-h">It remembers you</p>
          <div class="ys-chips"><span>Knee pain on deep squats</span><span>Trains before work</span><span>Vegetarian</span><span>45 minutes, three days</span><span>Dumbbells at home</span></div>
          <p class="ys-mem-p">Your answers, limits and preferences live in your profile. The plan never programs a movement you asked it to avoid, and the Coach reads your profile and history before every answer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ys-stage app">
        <div class="ys-sw" role="tablist" aria-label="Example athletes">
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-a="0">Kabir, 22</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-a="1">Anita, 45</button>
          <i class="ys-sw-pill" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="ys-card" data-ys aria-live="polite"></div>
        <p class="demo-note">Two example athletes. Plans simplified.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="complete" aria-labelledby="complete-h">
    <h2 class="sec-h disp cx-h" id="complete-h"><span class="h-a">Five apps that never talk to each other.</span><span class="h-b">One app that sees your whole day.</span></h2>
    <p class="sec-sub">A workout log, a food diary, a sleep app, a recovery band. Tracend puts them in one place, reads them together, and adds a Coach that knows all of it.</p>
    <div class="bento">
      <figure class="tile t-train"><span class="was" aria-hidden="true"><s>Workout log app</s></span><div class="shell app" data-tile="training"></div><figcaption><b>Training</b>Every set, rep, load and effort. New bests called out.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="tile t-rec"><span class="was" aria-hidden="true"><s>Recovery band app</s></span><div class="shell app" data-tile="recovery"></div><figcaption><b>Recovery</b>HRV, resting heart rate, sleep and breathing, against your own normal.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="tile t-food"><span class="was" aria-hidden="true"><s>Food diary app</s></span><div class="shell app" data-tile="food"></div><figcaption><b>Food</b>Snap a meal. Protein and calories, confirmed by you.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="tile t-sleep"><span class="was" aria-hidden="true"><s>Sleep app</s></span><div class="shell app" data-tile="sleep"></div><figcaption><b>Sleep</b>Read from your watch while you sleep.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="tile t-prog"><span class="was" aria-hidden="true"><s>Weight app</s></span><div class="shell app" data-tile="progress"></div><figcaption><b>Progress</b>Weight and strength over months, not days.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="tile t-coach"><span class="was" aria-hidden="true"><s>Chatbot that never saw your data</s></span><div class="shell app" data-tile="coach"></div><figcaption><b>Coach</b>Ask why. Every answer uses your own numbers.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <p class="own"><span><b>Nothing new to buy.</b> It reads the iPhone you already own, and your Apple Watch if you wear one. For iPhone, best with Apple Watch; Android and other smartwatches are in testing.</span><span><b>Nothing changes without your OK.</b> Every change to your plan shows its evidence and waits for you to approve it. Each approved plan is saved as a new version.</span><span><b>Your plan keeps working</b> when the AI, Apple Health or the network is down.</span></p>
  </section>


  <section class="sec wrap" id="body" aria-labelledby="body-h">
    <div class="bm">
      <div class="bm-copy">
        <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="body-h">Every workout, mapped to your body.</h2>
        <p class="sec-sub">Your plan, day by day, on the app&rsquo;s muscle map. Every set counts toward the muscles it works, so you see what the week covers and what it skips.</p>
        <div class="wk" role="tablist" aria-label="Example week">
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-d="0"><b>Mon</b><span>Legs</span><em>Done</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-d="1"><b>Tue</b><span>Pull</span><em>Today</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-d="2"><b>Thu</b><span>Push</span><em>Planned</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-d="3"><b>Sat</b><span>Arms, core</span><em>Planned</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bm-stage app" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="body-h"><div class="bm-in">
        <div class="bm-figs" aria-hidden="true"><svg data-v="front"></svg><svg data-v="back"></svg></div>
        <div><p class="bm-head" data-bm-head>Monday, done<b>Legs</b></p><ul class="bm-list" data-bm-list></ul></div>
      </div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="coach" aria-labelledby="coach-h">
    <div class="cc">
      <div class="cc-copy">
        <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="coach-h">Ask your Coach anything.</h2>
        <p class="sec-sub">It answers with your own numbers: your sets, your meals, your sleep. Then it shows the evidence it used, and what it could not see.</p>
        <div class="cq" role="group" aria-label="Example questions">
          <button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-q="0">Why lighter today?<i><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></i></button>
          <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-q="1">How did I eat yesterday?<i><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></i></button>
          <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-q="2">Am I still losing weight?<i><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></i></button>
        </div>
        <p class="demo-note" style="margin-top:18px">An example conversation for a made-up athlete.</p>
        <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-cc-live></p>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-dev" aria-hidden="true" data-cc-phone></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-h">
    <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="demo-h">Change the night. Watch the morning change.</h2>
    <p class="sec-sub">Move the sliders. This is how the recovery score and today&rsquo;s session respond, simplified for one example athlete.</p>
    <div class="demo-grid">
      <form class="controls"><div class="controls-in">
        <div class="ctl"><label for="d-sleep">Sleep last night <output for="d-sleep" data-o="sleep">6 h 12 m</output></label>
          <input id="d-sleep" type="range" min="240" max="540" step="6" value="372" aria-describedby="d-sleep-h"><small id="d-sleep-h">Sam usually needs about 7 h 20 m.</small></div>
        <div class="ctl"><label for="d-hrv">Morning HRV <output for="d-hrv" data-o="hrv">52 ms</output></label>
          <input id="d-hrv" type="range" min="30" max="80" step="1" value="52" aria-describedby="d-hrv-h"><small id="d-hrv-h">Sam&rsquo;s normal is 54 ms.</small></div>
        <div class="ctl"><label for="d-rhr">Resting heart rate <output for="d-rhr" data-o="rhr">58 bpm</output></label>
          <input id="d-rhr" type="range" min="48" max="72" step="1" value="58" aria-describedby="d-rhr-h"><small id="d-rhr-h">Sam&rsquo;s normal is 57 bpm.</small></div>
        <fieldset class="ctl"><legend>Yesterday&rsquo;s training</legend>
          <div class="seg" data-seg><button type="button" data-v="rest" aria-pressed="false">Rest</button><button type="button" data-v="easy" aria-pressed="false">Easy</button><button type="button" data-v="moderate" aria-pressed="false">Moderate</button><button type="button" data-v="heavy" aria-pressed="true">Heavy</button></div></fieldset>
      </div></form>
      <div class="demo-out app">
        <div class="a-card demo-today">
          <p class="a-kicker">Today, example</p>
          <p class="verdict" data-d="verdict">Under-recovered</p>
          <p class="reason" data-d="reason">Sleep less than usual, recent training higher than usual. Everything else is normal for you.</p>
          <div class="ringbox"><svg data-ring-demo aria-hidden="true"></svg><div class="ring-c"><span class="rl">Recovery</span><span class="sc a-num" data-d="score">36</span><span class="a-band" data-d="band">Low</span></div></div>
          <div class="chips" data-d="chips"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="a-card demo-plan">
          <p class="a-kicker">Today&rsquo;s session, Pull day</p>
          <p class="a-title" data-d="plan-head">Go lighter today.</p>
          <p class="reason" data-d="plan-body" style="color:var(--a-text)">Deadlift 3 &times; 3 at 140 kg, effort 7 at most.</p>
          <div class="lvl" aria-hidden="true" data-d="lvl"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        </div>
        <p class="demo-note">Simplified example. In the app, every reading is compared with your own rolling normal, and breathing rate counts too.</p>
        <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-d="live"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-h">
    <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="why-h">Other apps stop at the score. Tracend turns it into today.</h2>
    <div class="versus">
      <div class="shell"><div class="a-card vs-in app"><h3>A score</h3><p class="vs-q">You open a recovery app. It says 36.</p><div class="vs-ring"><svg data-ring-vs aria-hidden="true"></svg><b>36</b></div><p class="vs-now">Now what?</p></div></div>
      <div class="shell"><div class="a-card vs-in app"><h3>Tracend</h3><div data-vs-session></div><p class="vs-ok"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3.2 8.4l3 3 6.6-6.8"/></svg>Your plan only changes when you approve it.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

 <section class="sec wrap" id="next" aria-labelledby="next-h">
    <div class="nx">
      <div class="nx-copy">
        <p class="soon"><i></i>Coming next. Not in the beta yet.</p>
        <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="next-h">Log the set without opening the app.</h2>
        <p class="sec-sub">Start a workout, then lock your phone. Your session stays in the Dynamic Island and on the Lock Screen, and you log each set right there, at the weight and reps shown. Changing them takes the app. An Apple Watch app follows.</p>
        <div class="nx-steps" role="tablist" aria-label="What is coming next">
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-s="0"><b>01</b><span>Dynamic Island</span><em>Leave the app. The set stays one tap away.</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="1"><b>02</b><span>Lock Screen</span><em>Log the set, keep resting.</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="2"><b>03</b><span>Apple Watch</span><em>Log from your wrist. Your phone stays in sync.</em><span class="prog"><i></i></span></button>
        </div>
        <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-nx-live></p>
      </div>
      <div class="nx-dev" aria-hidden="true" data-nx></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap close" id="join" aria-labelledby="join-h">
    <div class="c-clock" aria-hidden="true" data-cclock></div>
    <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="join-h">See you at 18:40.</h2>
    <p class="sec-sub">Join the free beta. For iPhone, best with Apple Watch; Android and other smartwatches are in testing. We&rsquo;ll email you when your spot opens.</p>
